Date and time inputs open the HarmonyOS shell's picker on a phone.

ohos-native-pickers.patch turned InputMultipleFieldsUI off from the command
line, but InputMultipleFieldsUIWithPointerChecks (stable since M154) implies
it back on, so the input kept Blink's internal calendar. Do as Android does
instead: keep the input's look, and when kOhosExternalPopupMenus is on,
OpenDateTimeChooser always uses ExternalDateTimeChooser.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
and ohos-native-pickers.patch applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-shell-date-picker.patch

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/page/chrome_client_impl.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/page/chrome_client_impl.cc
index f44b9dc..bb219d5 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/page/chrome_client_impl.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/page/chrome_client_impl.cc
@@ -837,7 +837,14 @@ DateTimeChooser* ChromeClientImpl::OpenDateTimeChooser(
   // Android does not support PagePopup, so we must always use the native
   // picker.
 #if !BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
-  if (RuntimeEnabledFeatures::InputMultipleFieldsUIEnabled()) {
+  // On an OHOS phone (kOhosExternalPopupMenus) the shell's own picker
+  // answers, as Android's does; the input keeps its multiple-fields look, as
+  // on Android since InputMultipleFieldsUIWithPointerChecks.
+  if (RuntimeEnabledFeatures::InputMultipleFieldsUIEnabled()
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+      && !base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kOhosExternalPopupMenus)
+#endif
+  ) {
     return MakeGarbageCollected<DateTimeChooserImpl>(frame, picker_client,
                                                      parameters);
   }
